<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Champoeg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Champoeg was a settlement on the Willamette River in present-day Oregon, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, where settlers met on 2 May 1843 and voted narrowly to form a provisional government, by tradition 52 votes to 50. It was the first American-style government on the Pacific coast. The town was destroyed by a flood in 1861, and the site is now a state heritage area.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/champoeg.jpg" alt="Champoeg" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: M.O. Stevens · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Champoeg_State_Park_museum.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
